_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 18
---
order: 18
---
short_label: XI.18
---
statement: If a straight line is at right angles to any plane, then all the planes through it are also at right angles to the same plane.
---
proof:

Let any straight line *AB* be at right angles to the plane of reference.

I say that all the planes through *AB* are also at right angles to the plane of reference.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="290" height="220" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XI.18 diagram" src="propXI18.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "XI.18",
        elements: [
            "X;point;free;100000,200",
            "Y;point;free;200,-100000",
            "Z;point;free;30000,-100000",
            "P0;point;free;30,200;0;0,75,100",
            "P2;point;free;260,70;0;0,75,100",
            "P1;point;intersection;P0,X,P2,Z;0;0",
            "P3;point;intersection;P2,X,P0,Z;0;0",
            "P;polygon;quadrilateral;P0,P1,P2,P3;0;0;lightGray;brighter",
            "A;point;free;180,40",
            "B;point;lineSlider;A,Y,180,140",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "E;point;lineSlider;P1,P2,200,120",
            "C;point;intersection;E,B,P0,P3",
            "D;point;parallelogram;A,B,C",
            "DE;polygon;parallelogram;D,C,E;0;0;black;random",
            "F;point;lineSlider;C,E,100,150",
            "G;point;intersection;A,D,F,Y",
            "FG;line;connect;F,G"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Let the plane *DE* be drawn through *AB.* Let *CE* be the intersection of the plane *DE* and the plane of reference.

Take a point *F* at random on *CE,* and draw *FG* from *F* at right angles to *CE* in the plane *DE.* [!just I.11]

Now, since *AB* is at right angles to the plane of reference, therefore *AB* is also at right angles to all the straight lines which meet it and lie in the plane of reference, so that it is also at right angles to *CE.* Therefore the angle *ABF* is right. [!just XI.Def.3]

But the angle *GFB* is also right, therefore *AB* is parallel to *FG.* [!just I.28]

But *AB* is at right angles to the plane of reference, therefore *FG* is also at right angles to the plane of reference. [!just XI.8]

Now a plane is at right angles to a plane when the straight lines drawn in one of the planes at right angles to the intersection of the planes are at right angles to the remaining plane. And *FG,* drawn in one of the planes *DE* at right angles to *CE,* the intersection of the planes, was proved to be at right angles to the plane of reference. Therefore the plane *DE* is at right angles to the plane of reference. [!just XI.Def.4]

Similarly it can also be proved that all the planes through *AB* are at right angles to the plane of reference.

Therefore, *if a straight line is at right angles to any plane, then all the planes through it are also at right angles to the same plane.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
---
body:

This proposition is used in the proof of proposition @XII.17.
